        <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"><a id="ExecutiveSummary"><!--Anchor--></a>Executive Summary</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(18, 115, 153); font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; font-style: italic;">2025 Business Performance Highlights</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">In 2025, we continued to advance our vision of becoming the world&#8217;s leading beauty, wellness and lifestyle leadership opportunity platform. We were
          able to lay the groundwork for our two major growth initiatives for 2026: launching our Prysm iO intelligent wellness platform and expanding into India. We finished 2025 with $1.49 billion in revenue, which included a negative foreign currency
          impact of 0.8%, or $13.4 million, and an improved earnings per share over 2024.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">We delivered results within our previously communicated guidance range and grew earnings per share through disciplined cost management and operational
          execution, as well as the sale of our Mavely business. Notably, our core Nu Skin gross margin expanded to 77.4% for the full year, reflecting progress in product mix and efficiency initiatives.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">During the year, we also generated positive operating cash flow, reduced outstanding debt and further strengthened our balance sheet. In January 2025,
          we completed the sale of the Mavely business for a total transaction value of $250 million, and proceeds from the transaction were used to pay down debt and support continued investment in innovation. While transitioning our business to enable
          our two strategic growth priorities has come with some inherent switching costs as our company and channel realign business practices, we believe these shifts are critical to our mid- to long-term success. As we pursue these strategic growth
          priorities, we will continue to drive our third critical priority of improving operational performance and efficiency to return value to stockholders.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(18, 115, 153); font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; font-style: italic;">2025 Compensation Changes</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">In the first quarter of 2025, we reduced the base salaries of each of our NEOs in light of our financial performance and broader cost management
          initiatives. We also reduced the CEO&#8217;s target bonus percentage. Mr. Keisel was promoted to be our EVP and President of Global Sales effective March 2024. Given his recent promotion, his base salary was subsequently increased to ensure retention
          and alignment with competitive roles. For more information about these changes, see &#8220;Base Salary&#8221; and &#8220;Cash Incentive Bonuses,&#8221; below.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div class="BRPFPageBreakArea" style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;">
          <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">19</span></div>

          <div class="BRPFPageBreak" style="page-break-after: always;">
