        <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">Calculation of Bonus: Achievement of Performance Goals and Potential Adjustment
            for Individual Performance.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> The precise percentage of target bonus that a participant earns is based on the degree to which pre-determined performance levels
            are met or exceeded for the year. Participants may earn between 25% and 200% of their target bonus opportunity attributable to each goal based on performance against established minimum, goal and stretch performance levels, with payouts
            determined on a linear interpolation basis between such levels. If the minimum adjusted operating income threshold is not achieved, then (1) no payout is made with respect to the adjusted revenue metric; and (2) any payout for achievement of
            the strategic goals is capped at 25% of the participant&#8217;s target bonus opportunity.</span></div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Notwithstanding the above methodology, the Committee may adjust an executive&#8217;s bonus based on factors it considers relevant, including individual
          performance and certain compliance-related objectives.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">Establishment of Performance Goals.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> In establishing the performance levels in our Executive Cash Incentive Plan, the Committee considers various factors, including our recent performance and current business plans; general business
            and economic conditions; business risks; and our company&#8217;s business objectives, which for 2025 focused on growth in our business, improving our affiliate-focused programs, optimizing our product portfolio, refining our digital ecosystem and
            strengthening our Rhyz strategic investment arm. After considering these factors, the Committee set the 2025 performance goals that are described below.</span></div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Our 2025 Executive Cash Incentive Plan was based on achievement of goals related to adjusted revenue, adjusted operating income and strategic goals.
          The adjusted revenue and adjusted operating income metrics were equally weighted, totaling 75%, because management is responsible for both growing the business and increasing profitability, including control of expenses. The strategic goals were
          weighted at 25% to drive key company strategies for future growth and stockholder value.</div>

        <div>&#160;</div>

        <div class="BRPFPageBreakArea" style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;">
          <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">25</span></div>

          <div class="BRPFPageBreak" style="page-break-after: always;">
