              </div>

            </div>

          </div>


          <ix:nonNumeric name="ecd:CompActuallyPaidVsCoSelectedMeasureTextBlock" id="Text_cea18149691a4c02bbce4e4a4fc29be3" contextRef="c20250101to20251231" escape="true" continuedAt="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc1">
<div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">The following chart depicts the relationship between the &#8220;compensation actually paid&#8221; to our NEOs and our Adjusted EPS.</div>
</ix:nonNumeric>
          <ix:continuation id="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc1" continuedAt="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc2">
<div>&#160;</div>
</ix:continuation>
          <ix:continuation id="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc2" continuedAt="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc3">
<div style="text-align: center;"><img height="340" width="618" src="image00008.jpg" alt="graphic" style="height: 340px; width: 618px;"/></div>
</ix:continuation>
          <ix:continuation id="Text_d3e421f4d3e44940a365bc673954b2dc3">
<div>&#160;</div>
</ix:continuation>

          <div class="BRPFPageBreakArea" style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;">
            <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">50</span></div>

            <div class="BRPFPageBreak" style="page-break-after: always;">
              <hr style="margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; border-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear: both;"/></div>

            <div style="width: 100%;" class="BRPFPageHeader">
              <div><a href="#TABLEOFCONTENTS"><span style="font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;">Table of Contents</span></a></div>

            </div>

          </div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(18, 115, 153); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"><a id="PROPOSAL2"><!--Anchor--></a>PROPOSAL 2:<span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial;"><br/>
            </span>ADVISORY VOTE TO APPROVE OUR EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION</div>

          <div>
            <hr style="height: 1px; width: 100%; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; text-align: left; border: none; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: auto;"/></div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Pursuant to Section 14A of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, we are requesting stockholder approval of a non-binding advisory
            resolution approving our NEOs&#8217; compensation as disclosed in this proxy statement.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Compensation Objectives and 2025 Pay for Performance</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">The following objectives of our executive compensation program support our recommendation to approve the compensation of our NEOs:</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&#8722;</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Our program helps us to successfully recruit, motivate and retain experienced and talented executives.</div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div> <br/>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&#8722;</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">We implement a pay-for-performance philosophy through the use of incentives that:</div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div> <br/>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 36pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">a.</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Are tied to corporate and individual performance;</div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div> <br/>
            </div>

            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 36pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">b.</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Align the financial interests of our executives with those of our stockholders; and</div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div><br/>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 36pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">c.</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Are intended to drive superior stockholder value.</div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div><br/>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">The compensation program, which is administered by our Compensation and Human Capital Committee (the &#8220;Committee&#8221;), is intended to align actual
            compensation payments to actual performance and to adjust upward during periods of strong performance and downward when performance is short of expectations.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">In 2025, we continued to advance our vision of becoming the world&#8217;s leading beauty, wellness and lifestyle leadership opportunity platform. We were
            able to lay the groundwork for our two major growth initiatives for 2026: launching our Prysm iO intelligent wellness platform and expanding into India. We finished 2025 with $1.49 billion in revenue, which included a negative foreign currency
            impact of 0.8%, or $13.4 million, and an improved earnings per share over 2024.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">We delivered results within our previously communicated guidance range and grew earnings per share through disciplined cost management and
            operational execution, as well as the sale of our Mavely business. Notably, our core Nu Skin gross margin expanded to 77.4% for the full year, reflecting progress in product mix and efficiency initiatives.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">During the year, we also generated positive operating cash flow, reduced outstanding debt and further strengthened our balance sheet. In January
            2025, we completed the sale of the Mavely business for a total transaction value of $250 million, and proceeds from the transaction were used to pay down debt and support continued investment in innovation. While transitioning our business to
            enable our two strategic growth priorities has come with some inherent switching costs as our company and channel realign business practices, we believe these shifts are critical to our mid- to long-term success. As we pursue these strategic
            growth priorities, we will continue to drive our third critical priority of improving operational performance and efficiency to return value to stockholders.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Our executive compensation program and the pay-for-performance incentives that are built into it are key drivers of management&#8217;s motivation to
            achieve long-term growth in our business.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&#8722;</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">2025 compensation was predominantly variable.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> Consistent with our commitment to pay for performance, our CEO&#8217;s 2025 target compensation consisted of 85% variable compensation (cash incentive bonus and
                        equity awards) and 15% fixed compensation (salary and all other compensation). Our other NEOs&#8217; target compensation was 76% variable and 24% fixed.</span></div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div> <br/>
            </div>

            <div style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" class="BRPFPageBreakArea">
              <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">51</span></div>

              <div style="page-break-after: always;" class="BRPFPageBreak">
                <hr style="border-width: 0px; clear: both; margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000;"/></div>

              <div style="width: 100%;" class="BRPFPageHeader">
                <div><a href="#TABLEOFCONTENTS"><span style="font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;">Table of Contents</span></a></div>

              </div>

            </div>

          </div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&#8722;</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">2025 annual cash incentive and equity awards were aligned with
                        Company performance. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);">The annual cash incentive and annual equity awards that were provided to our NEOs for 2025 also reflect our
                        pay-for-performance philosophy. During 2025, we continued to face macroeconomic pressures in our core Nu Skin segments, which negatively impacted consumer spending and customer acquisition. In addition, while we continue to make
                        progress on our long-term vision, we have experienced headwinds from the transformation process. As a result, our adjusted revenue and adjusted operating income results in our Executive Cash Incentive Plan fell below the minimum
                        performance levels established at the beginning of the year, and consistent with our commitment to pay for performance, the cash incentive awards associated with our financial goals were not earned. A cash incentive award at 22% of
                        target was earned under our Executive Cash Incentive Plan based on partial achievement of our strategic goals. For the long-term incentive component of the compensation program, our 2023 PRSUs were not earned, our 2024 PRSUs were
                        partially earned and our 2025 PRSUs were earned at the maximum level.</span></div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
            <div> <br/>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div>
            <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="DSPFListTable" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; width: 100%; text-align: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); border-spacing: 0;">


  <tr>

    <td style="width: 18pt;">&#160;</td>

    <td style="width: 18pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: right;">
                    <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">&#8722;</div>
                  </td>

    <td style="width: auto; vertical-align: top;">
                    <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">2025 adjustments to salary and target bonus percentage. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);">In the first quarter of 2025, we reduced the base salaries of each of our NEOs in light of our financial performance and broader cost management initiatives. We
                        also reduced the CEO&#8217;s target bonus percentage. Mr. Keisel&#8217;s base salary was subsequently increased due to considerations related to retention and market competitiveness.</span></div>
                  </td>

  </tr>


</table>
          </div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"> <br/>
          </div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Advisory Resolution</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">The Board of Directors recommends that stockholders approve the following advisory resolution:</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; margin-left: 36pt; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">RESOLVED, that the stockholders hereby approve the compensation of the company&#8217;s named executive officers, as disclosed in this
            proxy statement pursuant to Item 402 of Regulation S-K, including the Compensation Discussion and Analysis, compensation tables and narrative disclosure.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Although this advisory resolution is non-binding, the Board values input from stockholders. The Board will consider the voting results for this
            proposal in making future compensation decisions.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">We currently intend to include a stockholder advisory resolution on our executive compensation program at our annual meeting of stockholders each
            year.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS RECOMMENDS THAT STOCKHOLDERS VOTE &#8220;FOR&#8221; THE APPROVAL OF THE ADVISORY RESOLUTION APPROVING OUR EXECUTIVE
            COMPENSATION.</div>

          <div><br/>
          </div>

          <div class="BRPFPageBreakArea" style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;">
            <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">52</span></div>

            <div class="BRPFPageBreak" style="page-break-after: always;">
              <hr style="margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; border-width: 0; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; clear: both;"/></div>

            <div style="width: 100%;" class="BRPFPageHeader">
              <div><a href="#TABLEOFCONTENTS"><span style="font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;">Table of Contents</span></a></div>

            </div>

          </div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(18, 115, 153); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;"><a id="PROPOSAL3"><!--Anchor--></a>PROPOSAL 3:<span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial;"><br/>
            </span>APPROVAL OF AMENDED AND RESTATED 2024 OMNIBUS INCENTIVE PLAN</div>

          <div>
            <hr style="height: 1px; width: 100%; color: #000000; background-color: #000000; text-align: left; border: none; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: auto;"/></div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">The Board of Directors (the &#8220;Board&#8221;) and the Compensation and Human Capital Committee (the &#8220;Committee&#8221;) have approved and adopted an amendment and
            restatement of the Amended and Restated 2024 Omnibus Incentive Plan (the &#8220;Amended Plan&#8221;) primarily to increase the number of shares authorized under the Amended Plan by 2,850,000 shares, subject to stockholder approval at the Annual Meeting.
            The Amended Plan is intended to continue our long-term equity compensation program, currently implemented under our existing Amended and Restated 2024 Omnibus Incentive Plan (the &#8220;Plan&#8221;), which was last amended effective May 29, 2025. The NYSE
            listing standards require us to obtain stockholder approval of the Amended Plan.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">We believe equity ownership provides an important link between the interests of long-term stockholders and our executives, managers and employees by
            rewarding the creation of long-term stockholder value. To meet this objective, equity awards are a critical component of our compensation program. Our primary reason for adopting the Amended Plan and recommending it for stockholder approval is
            to increase the number of shares available for equity compensation awards over the number that remain available under the Plan, which is currently the only incentive plan under which we grant equity awards to our directors, executive officers
            and employees.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">If our stockholders approve the Amended Plan at the Annual Meeting, it will become effective as of the date of such stockholder approval. Our
            directors and executive officers may have an interest in the approval of the Plan because they are eligible for awards under the Plan.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Why Stockholders Should Vote to Approve the Amended Plan</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">The additional shares are critical to our ability to continue to grant equity
              awards to eligible participants and to attract and retain valuable employees and directors.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> The Committee and the Board believe that our executive and
              employee compensation programs, and particularly the granting of equity awards, allow us to align the interests of our executives and other employees who are selected to receive awards with those of stockholders by rewarding long-term
              decision-making and actions for the benefit of the Company. Our equity plan is broad-based with a significant percentage of our awards being granted to employees below the executive officer level. We believe equity compensation assists in the
              attraction and retention of qualified executive officers and other employees and provides them with additional incentive to devote their best efforts to pursue and sustain our long-term performance, enhancing the value of the Company for the
              benefit of its stockholders.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">To keep us accountable to our stockholders, we are asking for approval for
              approximately one year&#8217;s worth of shares under the Amended Plan.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> The Committee considered that the shares currently available for issuance will not be
              sufficient to cover the equity awards that we would plan to grant in the next 12 months, especially if material fluctuations in our stock price continue to occur (which impacts the number of shares we grant, as we determine the size of equity
              awards based on the dollar value to be delivered to plan participants) and given the Company&#8217;s recent grant history. We consider equity compensation to be a vital element of our employee compensation program. We believe that, if stockholders
              approve the Amended Plan, the additional shares reserved will be sufficient to provide equity awards at appropriate levels for </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(118, 113, 113);">approximately one year.
              However, the actual duration of the share reserve will depend on factors that cannot presently be determined, such as the Company&#8217;s future stock price, changes in participation, our hiring and promotion activity, award type mix and levels,
              competitive market practices, acquisitions and divestitures, the rate of returned shares due to forfeitures, and how we choose to balance total compensation between cash and equity-based awards.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" class="BRPFPageBreakArea">
            <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">53</span></div>

            <div style="page-break-after: always;" class="BRPFPageBreak">
              <hr style="border-width: 0px; clear: both; margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000;"/></div>

            <div style="width: 100%;" class="BRPFPageHeader">
              <div><a href="#TABLEOFCONTENTS"><span style="font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;">Table of Contents</span></a></div>

            </div>

          </div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">Approval of the Amended Plan avoids disruption in our compensation programs
              and mitigates the need for significant cash compensation. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(118, 113, 113);">The Plan is the Company&#8217;s only active employee equity plan, and as of March 9, 2026, we had
              approximately 161,156 shares remaining for issuance under the Plan. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);">If our stockholders do not approve the Amended Plan, and as a consequence we are not
              able to continue to grant equity awards at competitive levels, we believe it will negatively affect our ability to recruit and retain highly qualified employees, which could have the effect of hampering our growth. If the Amended Plan is not
              approved by stockholders at the Annual Meeting, awards may continue to be granted using the remaining share reserve under the Plan until its expiration date in accordance with its terms. However, given the limited number of shares remaining
              available under the Plan, if the Amended Plan is not approved and the share reserve under the Plan is depleted, we would need to replace components of compensation previously awarded in equity with cash or with other instruments that may not
              necessarily support our goals of strengthening longer-term retention and aligning employee interests with those of our stockholders. Additionally, replacing equity with cash would increase our cash compensation expense and significantly
              deplete cash otherwise available that could be better used for operations, investment in our business, stock repurchases and other strategic purposes. For example, during 2025, we repurchased approximately two million shares. A portion of
              this repurchase program was used to offset dilution from our equity compensation plans.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">We followed a methodical process in determining our share reserve request.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> In setting the proposed number of shares that would be reserved and issuable under the Amended Plan, the Committee considered several factors, including the potential
              dilutive effect of shares remaining under the Plan and current equity awards outstanding under the Plan, the Company&#8217;s historical equity usage and expected compensation needs during the next 12 months, the expected dilution of the Amended
              Plan, and </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(118, 113, 113);">information published by institutional investors and advisors, including their proxy voting guidelines.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">The additional shares support our pay-for-performance philosophy and provide
              motivation to achieve our company&#8217;s vision.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> A significant portion of our executives&#8217; total compensation is equity compensation tied to the achievement of our
              business results. In 2025, equity compensation constituted 71% and 57% of the target compensation for our CEO and our other named executive officers, respectively. Such equity compensation promotes stock ownership and helps create alignment
              between our executives and stockholders. We use incentive compensation to help reinforce desired business results to our executives and other employees and to motivate them to make decisions to produce those results. If the Amended Plan is
              approved, it will continue to support our pay-for-performance philosophy.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">The additional shares provide motivation to achieve our company&#8217;s vision.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(101, 102, 106);"> Approval of the Amended Plan is critical to motivating our employees to continue advancing our vision of becoming the world&#8217;s leading beauty, wellness and lifestyle
              leadership opportunity platform. We have faced industry and company headwinds in recent years, as reflected in our stock price, and as a result, we have had to grant an increasing number of shares to achieve competitive compensation levels
              that motivate our employees to pursue our vision. For 2025, we are pursuing two strategic growth priorities related to our vision: launching our Prysm iO intelligent wellness platform and expanding into India. We also continue to drive our
              third critical priority: improving operational performance and efficiency to return value to stockholders. Incentive compensation, including the availability of continued equity compensation in the coming 1&#8211;2 years, is an important motivator
              for our executives and employees to continue pursuing these priorities.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-style: italic; color: rgb(18, 115, 153);">The size of our share reserve request Is reasonable.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; color: rgb(118, 113, 113);"> If the stockholders approve the Amended Plan, then as of May 28, 2026, we would have an additional 2,850,000 shares available for future grants of awards, for a total of
              3,011,156 shares available for grants under the Amended Plan (as adjusted by shares subject to awards granted under the Plan or returned to the Plan between March 9, 2026 and the date of the 2026 Annual Meeting). In addition, as described in
              the &#8220;Share Reserve&#8221; section below, certain shares subject to awards granted under the Prior Plan may become available for grant under the Amended Plan.</span></div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">Our equity plan dilution rate (or overhang) as of March 9, 2026 was 10.5%. If shareholders approve the Amended Plan, the addition of 2,850,000 new
            shares under the Amended Plan would increase our dilution rate to 14.9%. For further details about these calculations, see the Fully-Diluted Overhang Calculation table below.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">In sum, to ensure that we can continue to attract, motivate and retain highly qualified talent and to maintain a vitally important compensation tool
            aligned with stockholder interests, the Board recommends that our stockholders vote for the approval of the Amended Plan.</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="clear: both; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;" class="BRPFPageBreakArea">
            <div style="text-align: center;" class="BRPFPageNumberArea"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal;">54</span></div>

            <div style="page-break-after: always;" class="BRPFPageBreak">
              <hr style="border-width: 0px; clear: both; margin: 4px 0px; width: 100%; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000;"/></div>

            <div style="width: 100%;" class="BRPFPageHeader">
              <div><a href="#TABLEOFCONTENTS"><span style="font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;">Table of Contents</span></a></div>

            </div>

          </div>

          <div style="text-align: left; color: rgb(47, 84, 150); font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Key Data&#8212;Outstanding Awards, Share Usage and Dilution</div>

          <div>&#160;</div>

          <div style="text-align: justify; color: rgb(101, 102, 106); font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">As of March 9, 2026, we had the following awards granted and outstanding, and only 161,156 shares remaining available for future awards under the
            Plan:</div>

